---
import Base from '@app/layouts/Base.astro';
import { DocAside } from '@core';
---
<Base title="Ecosystem" description="Honest status of Visual Spec tooling and adapters.">
  <div class="container doc-layout">
    <DocAside current="ecosystem" />
    <div>
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Status</div>
      <h1>Ecosystem</h1>
      <p>What this repository ships today, and what remains an interoperability idea rather than a product claim.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <article class="resource-card">
        <div class="mono"><span class="status-dot"></span>SHIPPED</div>
        <h3>Specification &amp; JSON Schema</h3>
        <p>Normative text, modular Draft 2020-12 schemas, profile constraints, examples and checksums live in this repository and are published under <code>/schema/1.0/</code>.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/specification/1.0/">Read the specification <span>↗</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="resource-card">
        <div class="mono"><span class="status-dot"></span>SHIPPED</div>
        <h3>Validator CLI</h3>
        <p>Structural and implemented semantic checks run locally with <code>npm run validate -- &lt;file&gt;</code>. Schemas resolve from packaged files without fetching reference content.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/learn/conformance/">Conformance model <span>↗</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="resource-card">
        <div class="mono"><span class="status-dot"></span>SHIPPED</div>
        <h3>Generated pages</h3>
        <p>Agent-built HTML targets from the example documents. They illustrate consumption of Visual Spec, not runtime conformance or a full renderer.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/use-cases/">Browse use cases <span>↗</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="resource-card">
        <div class="mono"><span class="status-dot"></span>SHIPPED</div>
        <h3>Reference explorer</h3>
        <p>Build visual-reference descriptors and locators for websites, images, video, Figma, PDFs and more. It does not fetch or verify external sources.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/reference-explorer/">Open explorer <span>↗</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="schema-section">
      <h2>Adapters</h2>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>None shipped in this release.</strong> Platform mappings in the component catalog are informative design guidance. Visual Spec does not claim React, Swift, Unity or Android adapters are implemented.
      </div>
      <p>
        An adapter should begin with a capability declaration: the format versions, profiles, component kinds, layout modes, motion features and accessibility contracts it supports.
        Unsupported required capabilities must be reported rather than silently dropped. Approximations need an inspectable record of what changed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/learn/adapter-guide/">adapter guide</a> and propose normative interoperability changes through the <a href="/rfcs/">RFC process</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
